\f1\fs22 Gerry nodded. \'93And he\'92s just been rescued by a battalion of Elvi\'97by order of the so-called Holy Momma.\'94\
Dunhilton\'92s brain began to grind. \'93Who is this Holy Momma?\'94\
Gerry kept it carefully vague. \'93Elvi tradition, CEO. Their original Holy Momma was one Gladys Love, the original Elvis Presley\'92s mother. Grayling Corp programmed the veneration into their ELVIS units right from the start. Sometimes the clones get ceremonial, claim a Holy Momma is rallying them for this or that, but the title shifts with the mood or the year. If there\'92s a current claimant, we don\'92t know who it is. Could just be a new round of Elvi myth-making.\'94\
Dunhilton frowned, not sure who was being handled, him or the truth.\
Gerry sensed the moment shift. Time to seal it.\
\'93I need total resources. The only way this is controlled is if I have direct command. PAPER oversight for intelligence and logistics. TRAMPS for operations.\'94\
Dunhilton hesitated, whirring internally. \'93Done. It\'92s yours.\'94\
Gerry finally sipped his whisky and said nothing. In matters like these, silence was the most diplomatic lie.
